GIMP Palette
Name: KnockItOff — starter palette
Columns: 5
#
# REPLACE THIS. It is a working palette, not a good one for your game: three
# neutral-ish ramps that will render anything and commit to nothing.
#
# Every sample in this repo carries its own palette, and that is the whole
# reason nine games built on one library do not look like one game. Look at
# src/MonoGame.GameFramework.Roguelike/Content/sprites/palette.gpl for a
# palette that is doing real work — six steps of blue-grey and almost no hue,
# because at 60x34 tiles value *is* the level geometry.
#
# Two rules, both enforced:
#
#   * The first entry must stay exactly as it is. `outline` #1A1A1A is the one
#     colour every palette in the repo shares, and it is what keeps nine art
#     directions reading as one cast. check-palettes fails without it.
#
#   * No two colours may sit in the same hue family at the same lightness.
#     That is one ramp step drawn twice — invisible to the eye, recorded in
#     every file, and it turns "the mid blue" into a coin flip.
#
# Load it in Aseprite via Palette -> Load Palette, and set the sprite to
# Indexed colour mode: off-palette pixels then become unpaintable, which beats
# catching them at the gate.
#
